{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.isSafeBitVecWidth\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">isSafeBitVecWidth</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">w</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if bit-vectors of width `w` are safe to evaluate.\n\nMost bit-vector operations compute `2^w`. The bound `2^32` comes from the runtime, not the kernel:\n`lean_nat_pow` (`src/runtime/object.cpp`) aborts the process when the base is greater than `1` and\nthe exponent is greater than `UINT_MAX`, because `mpz::pow` takes the exponent as an\n`unsigned int`. Thus, procedures that evaluate bit-vector operations on literals must not build a\n`BitVec w` value unless this function returns `true`.","docLink":"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.isSafeBitVecWidth","kind":"def","line":85,"name":"Lean.isSafeBitVecWidth","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.lean#L85-L95"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.checkShiftLeft\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">checkShiftLeft</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">warning</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/CoreM.html#Lean.Core.CoreM\">CoreM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if `isSafeShiftLeft a n threshold`, where `threshold` is the value of the option\n`shiftLeft.threshold`. Otherwise, reports a warning and returns `false`.\nThis method ensures there is at most one warning message of this kind in the message log.","docLink":"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.checkShiftLeft","kind":"def","line":66,"name":"Lean.checkShiftLeft","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.lean#L66-L83"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.isSafeShiftLeft\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">isSafeShiftLeft</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">a </span><span class=\"fn\">n </span><span class=\"fn\">maxShift</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if the left shift `a <<< n` is safe to evaluate given the threshold `maxShift`:\n`a` is `0`, or `n` is `≤ maxShift` and fits in 32 bits.\n\nThe runtime implementation of `Nat.shiftLeft` aborts the process when the shifted value is not `0`\nand the shift amount does not fit in 32 bits. Thus, every procedure that evaluates a left shift of\nliterals whose shift amount is not bounded by a machine word size must use this function or\n`checkShiftLeft`.","docLink":"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.isSafeShiftLeft","kind":"def","line":54,"name":"Lean.isSafeShiftLeft","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.lean#L54-L64"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.shiftLeft.threshold\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">shiftLeft</span>.<span class=\"name\">threshold</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/Options.html#Lean.Option\">Lean.Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.shiftLeft.threshold","kind":"opaque","line":45,"name":"Lean.shiftLeft.threshold","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.lean#L45-L52"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.checkExponent\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">checkExponent</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">warning</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a> := <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool.true\">true</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/CoreM.html#Lean.Core.CoreM\">CoreM</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns `true` if `n` is `≤ exponentiation.threshold` and fits in 32 bits. Otherwise,\nreports a warning and returns `false`.\nThis method ensures there is at most one warning message of this kind in the message log.\n\nThe runtime implementation of `Nat.pow` aborts the process when the exponent does not fit in\n32 bits, even if the user increased `exponentiation.threshold`.","docLink":"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.checkExponent","kind":"def","line":24,"name":"Lean.checkExponent","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.lean#L24-L43"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">opaque</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.exponentiation.threshold\"><span class=\"name\">Lean</span>.<span class=\"name\">exponentiation</span>.<span class=\"name\">threshold</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Lean/Data/Options.html#Lean.Option\">Lean.Option</a> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.html#Lean.exponentiation.threshold","kind":"opaque","line":15,"name":"Lean.exponentiation.threshold","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/0b77e12952ad39077d80d8bd6b66d601f225c321/src/Lean/Util/SafeExponentiation.lean#L15-L22"}}],"imports":["Lean.CoreM"],"instances":[],"name":"Lean.Util.SafeExponentiation"}